hey 42 here lots of people go through a  rebellious phase at some point in their  teenage years i had several friends who  took up smoking for example and the guy  in my class at school got heavily into  death metal to get back at his parents  for forcing him to take flute lessons i  wasn't immune to this particular teenage  rite of passage either  you wouldn't think to look at me now but  for six months when i was about 14  i drank my tea without even using a  coaster  as shocking a crime as that may be it  pales in comparison to the cape as a  certain young american by the name of  coulson harris moore got up to during  what was quite simply the most  spectacular rebellious phase of all time  in fact calling it a rebellious phase  doesn't really do it justice  international crime spree would probably  be a better way of putting it  when the police finally caught up with  colton in 2010 he had a ten thousand  dollar bounty on his head and the  charges brought against him read more  like the plot for grand theft auto 6  than something a single human child  could ever actually have done in real  life  this is the frankly ridiculous story of  colton harris moore better known  as the barefoot bandit  all the best criminal masterminds have  an origin story and colton harris morse  is a particularly sad one that goes a  long way towards explaining how he came  to be one of the most prolific and  daring teenage criminals in history  before he acquired his intriguing  nickname more on that in a minute by the  way colton harris moore was just a kid  like any other growing up on kimono  island in the puget sound off the coast  of washington  according to most accounts colton's  childhood was pretty bleak he grew up in  a trailer nestled deep within one of the  many forests that can be found in the  center of camano island  and just to give you a taste of the kind  of vibe that was going on at home  at the bottom of the drive was a sign  reading  if you go past this point you will be  shot  yeah  colton's family was shall we say  dysfunctional his father was allegedly a  heroin addict he was sent to prison for  attacking colton when he was just 12  years old and his mother was an  alcoholic with a few so short she made  joe pesci's character in goodfellas  looks like a mormon  social services were called out to the  trailer as many as a dozen times during  colton's childhood  but for one reason or another nothing  ever came of it quite understandably  colton wasn't all that big a fan of  chilling out maxing and relaxing at home  and so from as young as seven he started  to sneak off into the woods often  staying there for days on end  the stealing that would come to  characterize pretty much the whole of  his young life started simply as a way  to stay alive  there was never much food in the fridge  at home and colton learnt early on that  other people's fridges were usually more  generously stocked he also stole  blankets clothes and other supplies to  help him survive during those long  nights he spent under the stars  when life at home got to be a bit too  much  in those early days colton wasn't  exactly the master thief he would become  in later life he was caught stealing on  multiple occasions with each misdemeanor  earning him a week or two in juvenile  detention  but as is often the case with most  things in life if you want to get really  good at stealing stuff a little practice  goes a long way  and boy did colton practice  it's hard to say exactly when he crossed  a line from i'm stealing this because i  need it into i'm stealing this because i  can  but soon enough colton was pilfering  pretty much everything that wasn't  nailed down to the floor  he was suspended from school numerous  times for stealing and his classmates  soon dubbed him klepto cult  by the time he turned 16 the scope scale  and frequency of colton's burglaries had  increased significantly and he was  routinely breaking into expensive  holiday homes that can be found along  kimono island's various beachfronts but  it was while breaking into one of these  in 2007 that he was caught red-handed  after neighbors spotted lights on in a  house that was supposed to be empty  and called the police  colton found himself facing no fewer  than 23 different charges of theft for  which he was ultimately sentenced to  four years in juvenile detention  [Music]  much to everyone's surprise klepto cult  seemed to change his ways during his  time inside  or at least he managed to convince those  in charge that he had because after  about 12 months he was transferred to a  minimum security facility to serve out  the remaining three years of his  sentence  with the benefit of hindsight i can  confidently say that minimum probably  wasn't quite the right kind of security  for a boy like colton  and soon enough he'd escaped  still only 17 at the time he would spend  the next two years living as a fugitive  during that time colton was almost  constantly on the move  only he knows exactly where he went and  when during that time  but he's thought to have traveled  through washington idaho south dakota  nebraska iowa illinois indiana and parts  of western canada  sometimes moving on foot and sometimes  stealing cars  he was rarely sighted but police were  able to piece together at least some of  his movements by the inevitable rash of  break-ins that would be reported  wherever he went  [Music]  despite these tantalising clues colton's  exact whereabouts remained frustratingly  difficult to pin down  in fact he may as well have been a ghost  what the police didn't know is that  colton had essentially become nocturnal  and was spending most of his time living  off the grid  only venturing into built-up areas to  steal what he needed to survive  well sort of he probably didn't need  that six thousand five hundred dollar  set of night vision goggles that he  bought using a stolen credit card but  hey you never know when something like  that might come in handy  especially when you're a nocturnal  fugitive  if coulson had been content to lay low  who knows how long he might have been  able to evade capture  but his natural caution was  counterbalanced by an almost alarming  willingness to take risks in order to  get what he wanted  he'd break into homes for the most  trivial of reasons to take along soak in  the bath or to watch tv  and if he found any given house to be  empty  sometimes he stayed there for days or  weeks on end  ordering survival gear to his borrowed  front door using stolen credit cards  but  of all the many crimes colton committed  during his time on the run  there's one that epitomizes his utter  fearlessness more than any other  stealing airplanes  colton was a self-confessed flight nut  and he stole his first plane a cessna  182s at the age of 17. the idea of a  teenager strolling into an airport and  nicking an airplane might sound pretty  crazy but it's positively insane when  you factor in the minor detail that the  first time he stole a plane klepto cult  had no idea how to actually fly one  in fact rumor has it he'd never even  been in a plane not even as a passenger  how the hell he managed to get that  cessna into the air and perhaps more  importantly back onto the ground again  afterwards is a genuine mystery to this  day  media reports from the time claim he  taught himself to fly through a  combination of reading manuals he bought  on ebay and practicing on flight  simulators but colton himself has  claimed he simply figured it out as he  went along  whatever the truth each flight was  meticulously planned and executed  colton would stake out an airport for  days on end before making his move  absorbing as much information as he  possibly could about airport security  shift patterns plane types and points of  entry  when he figured out which plane he  wanted to steal and how he'd spend weeks  figuring out a flight plan if he was  expecting to land during the night he'd  simply find a quiet airport and do  exactly that  but if he planned to land during the day  he'd use google earth to scan for likely  landing spots once he figured out where  he wanted to touch down colton would  digitally scout the surrounding terrain  so that when he was safely on the ground  he'd know exactly where to go next  something that was especially important  since a downed aeroplane in the middle  of a field was bound to attract police  attention fast  using these methods colton successfully  stole and flew no fewer than five  different aircraft during his time as a  teenage fugitive as word of these  outrageous antics began to hit the news  colton achieved genuine anti-hero status  particularly amongst young people with  facebook pages dedicated to the barefoot  bandit attracting tens of thousands of  followers  by the way if you're wondering what the  whole barefoot bandit thing was all  about the name came from reports that  colton liked to commit his various  crimes  sans shoes and socks  in truth that was more of an occasional  thing than a genuine modus operandi but  as his fame grew colton started to play  up to his moniker after breaking into a  grocery store in early 2010 he took the  time to draw dozens of feet on the floor  in chalk before making his escape  and he's known to have left at least one  enigmatic crime scene note that was  signed colton harris moore aka the  barefoot bandit  despite apparently enjoying his growing  notoriety it was starting to become a  bit of a problem the authorities weren't  overly impressed with the number of  rings that were being run around them by  an upstart teenager and the longer  colton remained at large the more  embarrassing the situation became in an  effort to ends the farce the police sent  sniffer dogs swat teams and helicopters  armed with infrared cameras after him  none of these methods proved effective  but colton must have realized the noose  was tightening around his neck  which is probably why he decided it was  time to make one last bold play  the first signs of what that play  involved came with reports at a plane  stolen from an airport in bloomington  indiana had been located apparently  abandoned by the person who'd taken it  most of colton's flights to this point  had been fairly short usually no further  than to a neighboring state  but this time was different  because the people who found the  abandoned airplane weren't from ohio or  illinois  in fact  they weren't even american  colton harris moore the barefoot bandit  a self-taught pilot with no formal  navigation training had flown a tiny  single engine aeroplane more than 1  200 miles to the bahamas  specifically to the island of great  abaco  as was usually the case when colton  showed up somewhere soon enough the  locals started noticing things going  missing with dozens of houses and  businesses reporting break-ins in quick  succession colton had become so famous  at this point that it wasn't long before  pretty much everyone on the island knew  the barefoot bandit was in town plenty  of people were upset  but plenty of others were flat out  excited one local girl even attempted to  secure a date with colton through his  ever expanding facebook fan page  and considering the fact that one of the  few times he was sighted on the island  was whilst buying a drink for a girl in  a bar  it's possible he actually took her up on  the offer  but if the authorities in america had  been embarrassed by carlton's general  refusal to get himself caught like a  normal person  it's safe to say they were positively  [ __ ] bricks at the force of him  flaunting their inability to apprehend  him on an international scale  the fbi promptly stuck a ten thousand  dollar bounty on his head to be paid out  to anyone who provided information that  led to his arrest flying to the bahamas  had been a bold some might say brilliant  move  but great abaco isn't a particularly big  place nor is its population all that  large  realistically the situation was only  ever going to end one of two ways  even with coulson's capture or his death  [Music]  during the epic james bond style  speedboat chase that brings this story  to an end  both of those possibilities seemed  equally likely  colton stole two different speedboats as  he sped from island to ireland with the  police in hot pursuit he's somehow  gotten his hands on a gun at this point  a fact that doesn't seem to have been  lost on the police  they rained down bullets on colton from  behind eventually shooting out the  engine on his boat and leaving him  stranded  for the first time in two years  colton found himself with nowhere to  hide  according to some reports when he  realized it was all over colton put a  handgun to his head and threatened to  end things on his own terms though  colton himself denies that part ever  happened  either way  he was brought in safe sound and  brilliantly barefoot  one of the first things the arresting  officers did was place a pair of  trainers on his feet almost as though  they thought by covering them up they  were robbing colton of whatever voodoo  it was that he'd been using to evade  america's finest for the previous two  years straight  for his antics in the bahamas colton was  sentenced to either three months in jail  or a 300 fine unsurprisingly he opted  for the latter but far weightier  punishments awaited him on his return to  america  where he was accused of committing  approximately a hundred different thefts  alongside a slew of other charges  like all trials of this magnitude there  was a lot of legal chewing and throwing  going on  but when the dust had settled colton was  sentenced to seven years in prison that  might sound like a fairly lenient  sentence considering all the fuss he'd  caused  but colton's extremely difficult  childhood was seen as a mitigating  factor in his subsequent crime spree as  was his age where many of the crimes  were committed  in the end he served fewer than five of  those years and on his release in 2016  the attorney who defended him during his  trial hired colton to work at his law  firm a solid indicator of just how much  good will colton had accumulated at this  point in spite of his remarkable career  as a teenage criminal  these days by all accounts he's an  upstanding member of society who's put  his rebellious teenage years firmly  behind him  though in 2016 his parole officer did  force colton to end a crowdfunding  campaign aimed at raising enough money  for him to get his pilot's license  too soon colton too soon  to this day the story of the barefoot  bandit remains a polarizing one and for  obvious reasons on the one hand colton  was an apparently heartless criminal  he practically turned stealing from  others into a game  on the other hand it's pretty hard to  blame someone with colton's upbringing  for going off the rails a bit  okay a lot  but still  colton genuinely does seem to want to  right the wrongs if his criminal past  he's even got a long way to paying off  the 1.4 million dollars in restitution  he owes to his many victims  thanks in no small part to selling his  story to 20th century fox for a seven  figure sum  hey i guess sometimes crime does pay  thanks for watching
 

